# .windsurfrules — Windsurf IDE Rules for Revit Development

- Target Scope: Autodesk Revit Add-in Development (C# / .NET)
- Single-threaded STA rule: All Revit API interactions must take place on the main thread via ExternalEvent if called from modeless UI or async contexts.
- Transaction rule: All database modifications require a committed Transaction wrapped in a using block.
- ElementId: Use ElementId.Value (Int64), not IntegerValue.
- Units & Parameters: Use ForgeTypeId with SpecTypeId and UnitTypeId via UnitUtils.
- Version Compatibility: Revit 2024 = net48; Revit 2025/2026 = net8.0-windows.
- Refer to skills/ and knowledge/ for detailed guidance.
